  "note": "DRAFT, needs review by a person. Maps farmer wording to fact records. Matching is longest-phrase-first, and a matched phrase is consumed so shorter phrases inside it cannot also match. Plain strings match as substrings (so Kannada suffixes still match); strings starting with '=' must be a whole word. Never add a generic word (worm, pest, disease, spray, medicine) as a pest/disease alias: that is exactly how a wrong-pest dose got through before (H-38). Symptom words (wilting, dead heart, bunchy top, whip) are deliberately NOT aliases: a symptom can have several causes, and mapping it to one disease's chemical would be diagnosis. organism_words (worm, pest, fly...) signal a pest/disease question: with no named subject the bot refuses, even if a topic keyword also matched, so a weed or fertilizer answer is never given to a pest question. Action words (spray, medicine) are deliberately not in that list. neutral_phrases (disease-free, earthworm...) are consumed first so they do not count as organism words.",
